<!--Post: 58--><!--Time: 1085340053-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST58"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitaboy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitaboy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 12:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->1.&#41; Julie Otero &#40;DOD 01-15-74&#41; and Kathryn Bright &#40;DOD 04-04-74&#41; worked on the same assembly line at Coleman. <BR> <BR>2.&#41; Michael Williams the supervisor from the same assembly line at Coleman was shot 4 days prior to the Otero murders. <BR> <BR>3.&#41; Michael Williams’s father was head of personnel at Coleman. He worked in the Human Resources Department, which was located at New York and Central. &#40;Approximately 1500 E Central&#41; <BR> <BR>4.&#41; Sherry Baker a 23 year old WSU student was murdered 11-12-74 at 603 New York. This is one of the top three cold cases that are similar to BTK. <BR> <BR>5.&#41; 603 New York is only a block away from the Coleman Human Resources Department. <BR> <BR>6.&#41; The Coleman factory at 2nd and St Francis is only 2 blocks from where BTK made the telephone call notifying police about Nancy Fox.  The Coleman Human Resources Department is only 8 blocks away from the telephone. <BR> <BR>7.&#41; What do you think? <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 58-->
<!--Post: 59--><!--Time: 1085346407-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST59"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 2:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->DThe Otero and Bright murders occured only 3 months apart.  I had never realized they were so close together.  I know that Mrs Otero had been laid off prior to her murder.  It seems logical that they both worked at Coleman has to be more then a coincidence.  I assume Wichita Police checked this angle, but didn&#39;t find a connection.  It still seems probable BTK knew the Oteros, but from Kevin Bright I&#39;m sure we would have heard if his sister knew their attacker, so , who knows?  Kevin Bright is giving KAKE tv an interview and it&#39;ll air on Tuesdays 10 oclock news.  Maybe he&#39;ll have new information that has been withheld from the public.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 59-->
<!--Post: 310--><!--Time: 1087875097-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST310"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 21, 2004 - 8:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe the human resources department should check their files for anyone with a gruge against the company. That&#39;s how they caught the Mad Bomber along with a profile.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 310-->
<!--Post: 319--><!--Time: 1087947370-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST319"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 22, 2004 - 4:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Since Julie Otero and Katherine Bright worked on the same &#34;line&#34; maybe their connection has something to do with the Transcontinental And Transport Company &#40;TAT&#41; also called the &#34;Lindbergh Line&#34;. March 17, St. Patrick&#39;s Day, and &#34;Lucky Lindy&#34;. New York to Los Angeles with a stop in Wichita. Otero had a son Charlie. Just a thought.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansasaviationmuseum.org/aerodrome/building.html" target=_top>http://www.kansasaviationmuseum.org/aerodrome/buil ding.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 319-->
<!--Post: 332--><!--Time: 1088114807-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST332"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitaboy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitaboy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 24, 2004 - 3:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just found out that Kevin Bright worked at Coleman also.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 332-->
<!--Post: 361--><!--Time: 1088475836-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST361"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Midtown<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Midtown<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 28, 2004 - 7:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know if the employees at Coleman wore uniforms at the time of the murders or prior to it?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 361-->
<!--Post: 364--><!--Time: 1088549178-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST364"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 29, 2004 - 3:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Was Mrs. Otero laid off anytime around Christmas? The initials of the family members that were killed are all JO. JO, JO, JO. In Spanish, that would be pronounced HO, HO, HO, HO. J sounds like H.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 364-->
<!--Post: 4396--><!--Time: 1106317200-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4396"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 6:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know if Coleman moved since the Oteros deaths? I ask because the photo of the Coleman building Tom took is of an abandoned building. What was there old address if they have moved?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4396-->
<!--Post: 5245--><!--Time: 1106970357-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5245"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 7:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kevin Bright began working for Coleman in March 1973 and quit in June to take a vacation.  Records show he was rehired to do the same job in July and quit in August.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5245-->
<!--Post: 5306--><!--Time: 1107042217-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5306"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 3:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Coleman Clothesline/Laundry Reel, a new thread started under General BTK Discussion, by a user with the name Dorothy.  I suspect that &#34;Dorothy&#34; is BTK.   The thread was posted kind of out of the blue, but also the syntax of the post looks similar to other posts that readers have suspected were by BTK &#40;under other user names&#41;.  The sentences are short, begin with lower case letters instead of upper case, some words are misspelled &#40;missing a letter here and there, BTK seems to do that with his letters to LE&#41;.   <BR> <BR>The time and day of the &#34;Dorothy&#34; postings make me suspect BTK is using this nom de plume as well -- Thursday in the afternoon, around 2-4pm, that&#39;s when BTK seems to make his other posts to this message board.  And of course &#34;Dorothy&#34; is a Kansan. <BR> <BR>One other thing about Dorothy&#39;s language caught my eye too -- the use of a detached tone and official -sounding language: &#34;per the Otero letter&#34; &#40;reminded me of &#34;that is correct&#34;...  <BR> <BR>When they catch BTK, I bet people who know him will say he says &#34;per the&#34; a lot in his everyday conversations. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5306-->
<!--Post: 5317--><!--Time: 1107047107-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5317"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 5:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Remember, Dorothy wasn&#39;t in Kansas ANYMORE!  Great thoughts Audrey.....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5317-->
<!--Post: 5323--><!--Time: 1107048981-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5323"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiquitah<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiquitah<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 5:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Audreyamw: I just posted to DOROTHY on that thread.  I thought the same thing! <BR> <BR>Same time frame and a Thursday.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5323-->
<!--Post: 5325--><!--Time: 1107050205-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5325"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 5:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Audreyamw, Dee, Chiquitah, <BR>Hi. You may or may not know this, but here goes. Tom has two other BTK boards with posters who are envious of his success at this site. Tom is also the webmaster of Zodiackiller.com. This site also has many disgruntled with Tom because Tom wouldn&#39;t help promote a recent &#34;suspect.&#34; The point is that there are a few score people who can &#40;and have&#41; easily register to use this site, solely to cause trouble. I had a problem with &#34;Dorothy&#34; once, too.  <BR> <BR>Some of the better posters here have already slowed or stopped posting. I&#39;m a decent poster, and a sincere one but I&#39;m tired of the same people, many using more than one name, attacking me. This is something which will happen to all of us for quite some time.  <BR> <BR>It&#39;s very discouraging to spend a lot of time writing an on-topic post which is thoughtful and valid, only to have a bunch of recently registered screen names tear it apart solely to cause trouble.  <BR> <BR>As for &#34;Dorothy&#34; being BTK, anything&#39;s possible but I believe BTK is brighter than this. &#34;Dorothy&#34; has posted many times and can easily be traced by the IP number.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5325-->
<!--Post: 5326--><!--Time: 1107050367-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5326"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 5:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Correction: second sentence should begin, &#34;Tom has <BR>to deal with people from two other BTK boards who are envious of his success at this site.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5326-->
<!--Post: 5364--><!--Time: 1107066067-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5364"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dorothy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dorothy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 10:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not BTK, and George -- when did you have a problem with me?  I&#39;ve only posted a very few times on this board.  Perhaps there was another Dorothy here at one time, I don&#39;t know. <BR> <BR>I simply posted about the Coleman clothesline, as a possible source for BTK&#39;s use of clothesline in the Otero murders.   <BR> <BR>I post on the C&amp;J forum as Theresnoplacelikehome.  That&#39;s who I am - just an old lady in TX.  Tom can attest to that with my registration.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5364-->
<!--Post: 5366--><!--Time: 1107066440-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5366"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 10:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dorothy. Sorry you&#39;ve experienced being trashed for no reason here. You should feel welcomed and free to discuss your opinions and insights. Ignore the bullies and continue to add your thoughts. We need some balance and new ideas. - Lily<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5366-->
<!--Post: 5368--><!--Time: 1107066758-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5368"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dorothy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dorothy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 10:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Lily... <BR> <BR>I think our imaginations get the best of us sometimes.  It&#39;s happened to me too - thinking so-in-so might actually be BTK. <BR> <BR>I truly doubt that BTK posts on any of the forums, knowing full well that his IP could easily be traced. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5368-->
<!--Post: 5381--><!--Time: 1107097590-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5381"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 7:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Homey, I am just glad guns are not issued with message board accounts!  Shoot first ask later.  How funny is that, people thinking you are BTK?  ROTFLMAO!!!  Now I have a better appreciation for the whole &#34;what constitutes a tip&#34; topic.   <BR> <BR>I am glad to know it is you, I will pay more attention to it.  How long have they been making those closelines?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5381-->
<!--Post: 5384--><!--Time: 1107099360-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5384"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 7:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dorothy:  Sorry for the mistaken identity. Darn, I thought I was onto something!  Lol-- At least it&#39;s a good lesson in how easy it is to go off on a wild goose chase. <BR> <BR>As for the trolls and other disruptive posters, I&#39;d hate to see a good forum like this one go dead because of that.  Like in Usenet, I think the best solution is to just ignore them.  Don&#39;t take the bait. <BR> <BR>I think the Coleman connection was a good point to bring up, though.  Too bad we don&#39;t have more details about where the clothesline may have come from.  I guess the clothesline may have been from a backyard clothesline, but if that were the case it would be difficult for BTK to access quickly -- those things are usually pretty high off the ground and are tied up tightly.  Maybe he brought it with him in his &#34;kit,&#34; the bag he apparently brought with him to at least one crime scene &#40;Viand&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5384-->
<!--Post: 5403--><!--Time: 1107108281-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5403"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dorothy - If BTK ever worked at Coleman, he may have had access to as much clothesline as he could hide and walk out with....Just a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5403-->
<!--Post: 5426--><!--Time: 1107116844-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5426"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dorothy - I was throwing in with Audrey, Dee and Chiquitah. Nothing more.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5426-->
<!--Post: 5428--><!--Time: 1107117119-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5428"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And there is a Coleman connection, yes. That&#39;s a pretty good thought, Lilymarie. The Otero letter indicates more than one type of rope or rope-like binding material...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5428-->
<!--Post: 5514--><!--Time: 1107153834-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5514"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiquitah<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiquitah<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry Dorothy....Just the way you said a few things, thats all. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5514-->
<!--Post: 5887--><!--Time: 1107444153-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5887"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 7:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK said to Kevin, something like &#34;havn&#39;t I seen you at the university?&#34; IF BTK worked at Colemans, could it be that that is where he knew Kevins face from? Kevin was only at Colemans for a short period and may never have remembered seeing BTK. How often does it happen that we see a face and struggle to remember where we know it from? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5887-->
